                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex 26]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Declaration by the United Kingdom Delegation on
                        Article 34</hi></head>
                <p>Mr. Jebb (United Kingdom) drew attention to the fact that, as recognised by the
                    Legal and Drafting Commission, multilateral conventions remained in force
                    irrespective of the outbreak of war. His Majesty’s Government accordingly took
                    the view that the Danube Convention of 1921 was still in force and would remain
                    in force until modified by common consent.</p>
            </div>
